        "original_id": "ba807ddb-b71c-53ec-afba-e0aa64e36d72",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Washington, D.C.\n- Organizations: St. Elizabeths Hospital, Providence Hospital, American Psychiatric Association\n- People: Winfred Overholser\n- Topics: Psychiatric hospitals, hospital history\n\nFacts:\n- St. Elizabeths Hospital opened in 1855 as the first federally operated psychiatric hospital in the United States.\n- Providence Hospital was founded in 1861 and is the longest continuously operating hospital in Washington, D.C.\n- Winfred Overholser was born in 1892.\n- Winfred Overholser was an American psychiatrist, served as president of the American Psychiatric Association, and was superintendent of St. Elizabeths Hospital for 25 years.\n- Winfred Overholser died on October 6, 1964.",
